{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dear Marie,\n\nI am now sitting in Elberfeld and writing to you from the quiet of the evening. Yesterday was full of impressions. In Bonn we visited Windischmann, and we spent some hours with Mr. von Schlegel. The paintings, especially the Dying Mary, have not yet let me go. The oyster with the Mosel wine was a small but pleasant enjoyment.\n\nThis morning I crossed the Wupper alone to Elberfeld. The sight of the students smoking their pipes there was a strange mix of youth and melancholy. It is a quiet area, but the thoughts here are not quieter, only differently ordered.\n\nThink of me when you instruct the boys about their duties; discipline is the foundation on which freedom later builds. I send you my regards and kiss you.\n\nYour\nG. W. F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795221280,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":177,"prompt_tokens":281,"total_tokens":458,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-doDBlSfWwcjZX3I5sRB5rbWNDHizJyVA","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":281,"prompt_ms":394.206,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.4028683274021352,"prompt_per_second":712.82527409527,"predicted_n":177,"predicted_ms":4116.244,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.387749999999997,"predicted_per_second":42.75742643050315}}